# PDF Batch Import (Admin)

Turn uploaded DSE question/solution PDFs into per-question cropped `IMG` assets. Admin Operations tool (after Question Ingestion). Backed by [app/pdf_import.py](mdc:app/pdf_import.py); reuses [app/batch_image_gen.py](mdc:app/batch_image_gen.py) for the atomic disk+DB write.

## Flow

```
stage (upload + rasterise) -> detect (SSE, vision LLM per page) -> [review] -> commit (SSE, crop + create rows)
```

- **Automatic mode**: detect SSE writes `plan.json`; on `done` the browser opens commit directly (reads `plan.json`).
- **Review mode**: after detect, a lightweight per-page editor (overlay boxes + crop-preview canvas) lets the admin **drag a box to move, drag handles to resize, Add box (draw on the page), edit qno, delete, click a crop thumbnail to enlarge it full-size (`showCropPreview`, native-res canvas overlay), or re-run a page with a different method/endpoint**. Boxes are edited in place on the in-memory `plan[kind]` items (`{page,qno,box,_uid}`); the live drag/draw system is in [templates/admin_pdf_import.html](mdc:templates/admin_pdf_import.html) (`startDrag`/`onDragMove`/`startDraw`/`finishDraw`/`applyBoxStyle`, pointer-events toggled via `.pdf-page-wrap.adding`). **Add/Delete auto-renumber** the following boxes (relative shift; see below); manual qno edits and move/resize do not. On Import the edited plan is POSTed to `/plan` (overwrites `plan.json`), then commit runs.

One **page image per LLM call** (keeps a small local model — e.g. `qwen3vl4b` — within its context window). Spanning questions = same `qno` on consecutive pages → grouped into a **multi-part** IMG asset (`replace_img_assets(..., stitch=False)`).

