## Routes (all `@admin_required`, gated on `AI_TOOLS_ENABLED`)

- `GET  /admin/pdf-import` — page (`pdf_import_page`).
- `POST /admin/pdf-import/stage` — multipart: `paper` (prefix `SUBJ_SOURCE_YEAR_PAPER`, PP only), `version`, `deskew` (default on), `que_pdf`, `sol_pdf` (≥1). Validates prefix + subject admin access. Rasterises pages (deskewing scans when set). Returns `{token, deskew, que:{pages}, sol:{pages}}`.
- `GET  /admin/pdf-import/page/<token>/<kind>/<int:page>.png` — serve a staged page PNG (kind = `que`|`sol`).
- `GET  /admin/pdf-import/detect?token=&endpoint_id=&method=&debug=` — SSE: per-page detection (QUE then SOL); accumulates `plan.json`. `method` ∈ `llm`/`refine`/`segment`. `debug=1` attaches `raw` (verbatim model reply) to each page event.
- `POST /admin/pdf-import/redo-page` — body `{token, kind, index, endpoint_id, method?, debug?}`; re-detect one page (optionally different method+endpoint) → `{boxes, raw?}`.
- `POST /admin/pdf-import/plan` — body `{token, plan:{que,sol}}`; sanitises + overwrites `plan.json`.
- `GET  /admin/pdf-import/commit?token=&version=&overwrite=` — SSE: crop + create rows from `plan.json`.
- `POST /admin/pdf-import/cancel` — body `{job_id}` (from the `job` SSE event).
- `POST /admin/pdf-import/discard` — delete the staging dir.

## SSE contract

Same shape as the other admin streams: `data: {json}\n\n`, types `job` (first; carries `job_id`) / `info` / `success` / `skip` / `error` / `done`. `detect` page events carry `page:{kind,index,boxes}`; `done` carries `stats` + `plan`. `commit` `done` carries `stats:{questions_created, assets_written, skipped, errors}`. Cancellation mirrors `app/ai_tools`: per-job `threading.Event` in `_PDF_CANCEL`, checked between pages/questions.

## Detection methods (`detect_page(config, png, atype, image_max_dim, method='llm')`)

Returns `(boxes, raw_text)`. Boxes are `{qno:int|None, box:[x1,y1,x2,y2] fractions 0..1, continues_prev, continues_next}`. `DETECT_METHODS = ('llm','refine','segment')`; threaded through `iter_detect`/`detect_single_page` and both routes. `_check_method_available` fails fast (one SSE error) when `refine`/`segment` are picked without NumPy.

- **`llm`** (default, no NumPy): the model returns tight boxes via `build_pdf_box_system`/`parse_question_boxes`. QUE prompt = tight box excluding answer space + margins **but keeping the marks annotation** (e.g. `(4 marks)`); SOL prompt = full solution incl. right-hand notes.
- **`refine`**: LLM boxes, then `pdf_layout.refine_box(gray, box, shrink_sides)` expands by `grow_frac` then trims to content via projection profiles (recovers chopped text / marks / figures, drops blank margins).
- **`segment`**: model returns only `{qno, y-start}` per item (`build_pdf_anchor_system`/`parse_question_anchors` — one scalar is far easier for a VLM to localise); `pdf_layout.segment_page(gray, anchors, shrink_sides)` derives each box from the whitespace gap to the next anchor.
- `shrink_sides = (atype=='QUE')` — SOL keeps full width so right-hand side-notes are never trimmed. CV runs on the **high-res** PNG (`load_gray`); the LLM still sees the downscaled copy.

**Deskew** (staging): `rasterize_pdf(..., deskew=)` straightens each scanned page in place via `pdf_layout.deskew_image` (projection-variance angle sweep ±6°, `expand=False` so dims/`meta` stay valid). Stored as `meta['deskew']`; skipped (warn) if NumPy missing.

**Coordinate convention is the #1 failure mode.** The prompt (`_PDF_BOX_JSON_CONTRACT`) pins an explicit **0–1000 integer grid, origin top-left, `[x1,y1,x2,y2]` (x-first)** with a worked example. `parse_question_boxes(text, img_w, img_h, coord_order)` (via `_normalize_box`) tolerates fences/prose and:
- **Axis order**: `coord_order='xyxy'` (default, Qwen/most) or `'yxyx'` (Gemma/Gemini/PaliGemma — vertical coord first), from setting `PDF_IMPORT_COORD_ORDER`. This is the only genuinely ambiguous part, hence a setting.
- **Range** (auto): `max≤1`→fractional; `max≤1024`→`/1000`; else raw pixels→divide by the **downscaled** dims the model saw (`_sent_image_size`, replicates `prepare_image`'s long-edge downscale to `LLM_IMAGE_MAX_DIM`), else `/max`.

**Debug**: `detect?...&debug=1` (and `redo-page` body `debug:true`) make `iter_detect`/the route log each page's verbatim reply and attach `raw` to the page event; the UI's **Debug** checkbox shows it in the console + a per-page collapsible. Use it to confirm the model's number range / axis order before flipping `PDF_IMPORT_COORD_ORDER`.

## Commit

`_group_plan(plan)` groups boxes by `(kind, qno)`, ordered by (page, top-Y). For each group: find-or-create `Question` (QID `{subj}_{source}_{year}_{paper}_Q{qno}`, `q_type` via `ingestor.determine_question_type`); skip if `slot_has_img` and not `overwrite`; else `crop_page` each part and `replace_img_assets(question, atype, version, imgs, stitch=False, source_path)` (atomic; fires DOC-thumbnail lifecycle). Boxes with `qno is None` are skipped.

`crop_page(png, box, pad_frac, trim_white, whiteness_threshold)`: pads the box by `pad_frac` (from `PDF_IMPORT_CROP_PAD_PCT`/100 — the "safety margin", larger = safer against clipping), crops, then white-trims back to content (keeps an 8px border; content never removed, so SOL side-notes stay). `whiteness_threshold` = `THUMBNAIL_WHITENESS_THRESHOLD`. The refine/segment CV params are `PDF_IMPORT_REFINE_GROW_PCT`/100 (`grow_frac`) + `PDF_IMPORT_ASSIST_PAD_PCT`/100 (`pad_frac`), read in `detect_page`.

## Staging

`OUTPUT_PATH/.pdf_import/<token>/` holds `meta.json` (subject/source/year/paper/version + `deskew` flag + page dims), `plan.json`, and `que/`/`sol/` (`source.pdf` + `page_NNNN.png`). `cleanup_old()` (called on each `stage`) purges dirs older than ~6 h; Discard removes one immediately. Token is validated (`^[0-9a-f]{8,40}$`) before any filesystem join.

## Auto-renumber (review, client-side)

Reading order within a kind = `(page, box top-Y)`. **Add** (`finishDraw`→`renumberAfterInsert`): the new box's qno = predecessor+1 (or 1), then every later box +1. **Delete** (`renumberAfterDelete`): every later box −1 (clamped ≥1). `refreshNumbersUI` rewrites labels + qno inputs from the plan. Re-detecting a page replaces its boxes with the model's authoritative numbers and does **not** cascade. Manual qno edits + move/resize never cascade (deliberate).

## Gotchas / invariants

1. Whole feature gated on `AI_TOOLS_ENABLED` + a vision-capable `LLMConfig` (detect/commit return an SSE error event otherwise).
2. Subject-admins only — the parsed prefix's subject is intersected with `get_user_admin_subjects()` in every route via `_pdf_load_token_meta`.
3. **PP only** (`DSE`/`CE`/`AL`); QB is out of scope. `section`/`level` left null (tagged later, like ingestion).
4. The LLM sees the **downscaled** page (`LLM_IMAGE_MAX_DIM`); crops are cut from the **high-res** page (`PDF_IMPORT_RASTER_WIDTH`). Boxes are fractional → resolution-independent.
5. `replace_img_assets` deletes existing IMG rows for the slot first — that IS the overwrite path. The skip-existing branch guards it with `slot_has_img` when `overwrite` is off.
6. Dev server must run threaded for the long SSE streams (already the case for the other batch ops).
7. **NumPy optional**: `refine`/`segment`/deskew need it (`pdf_layout.numpy_available()`); `llm` method + the rest of the app work without it. Detect fails fast with one SSE error; deskew silently skips with a warning. `segment` assumes a single column — dense MC / note-heavy SOL pages can over/under-merge; per-page retry to `llm` is the escape hatch.
